-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Additional notes (not part of the license terms above)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Scope
   The MIT License above covers TubeGet's own source code, artwork and
   documentation in this repository. It does not cover the third-party
   software listed below, which keeps its own license.

2. Third-party software
   - yt-dlp ............. The Unlicense
                          https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
   - FFmpeg ............. LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+ (depending on the build)
                          https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
   - Deno ............... MIT
                          https://github.com/denoland/deno
   - Qt for Python
     (PySide6) .......... LGPL-3.0
                          https://www.qt.io/qt-for-python
   - youtubedl-android .. GPL-3.0  (Android app only)
                          https://github.com/yausername/youtubedl-android
   - Python (bundled) ... PSF License
                          https://docs.python.org/3/license.html
   - Jetpack Compose,
     AndroidX, Coil ..... Apache-2.0  (Android app only)

   The Windows app downloads yt-dlp, FFmpeg and Deno at runtime; they are not
   part of this repository. The Android APK bundles youtubedl-android (which
   includes Python, yt-dlp, FFmpeg and QuickJS). Because youtubedl-android is
   GPL-3.0, the distributed Android APK as a whole is provided under the terms
   of the GPL-3.0. TubeGet's own code remains available under the MIT License,
   which is compatible with the GPL-3.0.

3. Responsible use
   TubeGet is a tool. Download only content that you own or have permission
   to save, and follow YouTube's Terms of Service and the copyright laws of
   your country. The authors are not responsible for how the software is used.

4. Trademarks
   "YouTube" is a trademark of Google LLC. TubeGet is an independent project
   and is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Google or YouTube.

